// A32 red-first row (0.0.253) — the FLOAT spill region must be INSIDE the frame.
//
// `main` below is float-heavy and its loop cannot fold (the block-boundary and
// terminator levers do not touch it), so `main` owns float vregs and, under
// 0.0.253, reserves the float spill region.
//
// THE DEFECT (0.0.252 and earlier): fspill_home(v) placed a float home at
//   -(48 + 8192 + (v+1)*8)     ~ 8 KB below %rbp
// while the frame formula reserved only
//   (48 + vreg_n*8), floored to 1024   == 1120 bytes for this program.
// So the FIRST time a float vreg was spilled to its float home it would have
// written ~8 KB below %rbp -- straight into the CALLER's frame. It is latent
// today only because the float allocator (fphys/fdef/fflush_all) had zero call
// sites (a float lived in a GPR and spilled to its INTEGER home). It is the
// hard prerequisite for F4 (xmm-resident FP) and for the vector spill region.
//
// THE FIX (0.0.253): fspill_home() is re-based to sit immediately BELOW the
// integer region (disjoint index range, derived from the SAME vreg extent), and
// codegen reserves fspill_size() for a function that uses floats. So `main`'s
// prologue frame GROWS by vreg_n*8 while an integer-only function's frame is
// byte-identical to 0.0.252.
//
// The gate stage (spillframe-guard) reads `main`'s prologue frame from the
// emitted object -- exact emitted bytes, load-independent, no tolerance.
//
// Hand-derived return (f2i truncates): sum_{i=0..63} i^2/(i+1)
//   = sum (i-1) + sum 1/(i+1) = 2016 - 64 + H(64) ~= 1956.74 -> 1956.
fn main() {
    let s = i2f(0)
    let i = 0
    while i < 64 {
        let x = i2f(i)
        s = faddf(s, fdivf(fmulf(x, x), faddf(x, i2f(1))))
        i = i + 1
    }
    return f2i(s)
}
